// === NATURAL_DISASTER ===

MERGE (pc:LexPlaycard {pointer: 'playcard:natural_disaster'})
SET pc.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    pc.title = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard',
    pc.summary = 'Natural-disaster disruption response policy for Tier-1 suppliers.';

MERGE (s:LexSection {pointer: 'section:natural_disaster:scope'})
SET s.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    s.role = 'scope',
    s.heading = 'Scope',
    s.order_idx = 0,
    s.text = 'This standard sets the immediate response to a **natural-disaster** disruption for the firm\'s top-ten Tier-1 suppliers. For each affected supplier it determines whether to replace, monitor, or maintain the relationship, the level to which the situation is escalated, and the response actions that may be taken while the disruption is live.\n\nThe standard covers the immediate response only. It does not assess commercial terms, cost, or contracts (Procurement); capacity, lead time, inventory, or demand planning (Supply Planning); supplier financial health (Supplier Risk); or sustainability and emissions (Sustainability). Those considerations inform longer-term sourcing decisions and are handled by the relevant functions, not in the immediate response set here.';

MERGE (s:LexSection {pointer: 'section:natural_disaster:bands'})
SET s.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    s.role = 'bands',
    s.heading = '1. Risk bands',
    s.order_idx = 1,
    s.text = 'Each affected Tier-1 supplier carries a composite risk score (`risk_score`, 0–1 scale) reflecting how broadly and deeply the disruption reaches the supplier, how dependent the firm is on it, and how central it is in the network. The score is banded as follows: a supplier is **HIGH** risk when its score is >=0.60, **MEDIUM** when 0.45–<0.6, and **LOW** when <0.45.\n\nThe composite score is assembled from five structural sub-scores — `sub_exposure_breadth` (breadth of downstream reach, tier-weighted), `sub_dependency_ratio` (concentration of the firm\'s reliance on this supplier), `sub_downstream_criticality` (operational importance of downstream operations fed by this node), `sub_node_centrality` (graph centrality of the Tier-1 node; high values mean failure propagates widely), and `sub_exposure_depth` (maximum disrupted tier, normalised) — each individually banded as **high** when >=0.66, **med** when 0.33–<0.66, or **low** when <0.33.';

MERGE (s:LexSection {pointer: 'section:natural_disaster:routing'})
SET s.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    s.role = 'routing',
    s.heading = '2. Activation and routing',
    s.order_idx = 2,
    s.text = 'This standard applies when the active disruption is a natural-disaster event. Where more than one type of disruption is active simultaneously, this type is addressed at priority 2 in the order geopolitical, natural disaster, cyber, economic, labour. The assessment runs in two passes, each working through provisions in order; the first provision whose conditions are fully satisfied takes effect and ends further checking within that pass.\n\nThe routing provisions below rely on network topology flags supplied by the Knowledge Graph query agent: `path_on_network` — whether the disruption intersects any path in the firm\'s supply network; `tier1_on_disrupted_path` — whether at least one scored Tier-1 supplier sits on a disrupted path; `shared_subtier_source` — whether two or more disrupted paths converge on a single lower-tier (Tier ≥ 2) node, revealing a hidden common point of failure; `count_disrupted_paths` — the number of distinct affected paths; and `tier1_in_region` — whether a supplier\'s primary site lies in the directly affected region.\n\n**Pass 1 — Scenario-level routing.** The provisions below apply once to the scenario as a whole, before any per-supplier assessment begins. If one fires, per-supplier evaluation does not occur. If none fires, proceed to Section 3.';

MERGE (s:LexSection {pointer: 'section:natural_disaster:decision'})
SET s.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    s.role = 'decision',
    s.heading = '3. Decision logic',
    s.order_idx = 3,
    s.text = 'Each Tier-1 supplier on a disrupted path is assessed against its composite risk band (Section 1) together with the structural sub-scores this disruption type keys on. The provisions below apply per supplier in the order listed; the first whose conditions are fully satisfied determines that supplier\'s response. Some provisions mix scenario-level facts (the same for every supplier) with supplier-level facts (assessed individually); where this occurs it is noted explicitly.';

MERGE (s:LexSection {pointer: 'section:natural_disaster:actions'})
SET s.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    s.role = 'actions',
    s.heading = '4. Permitted and prohibited actions',
    s.order_idx = 4,
    s.text = 'A response action may be taken during the live event only if it can realistically be put in place within the recovery window — that is, it relies on arrangements already in place before the disruption (pre-qualified alternates, standing buffer stock, contracted logistics flexibility). Structural measures that require building new capacity from scratch take longer than the recovery window allows and are deferred to the resilience roadmap.\n\nActions permitted during the live response:\n\n- activate a pre-qualified alternate source\n- intensify threat monitoring\n- run scenario lever generation\n- draw down strategic buffers\n- convene the Crisis Response Centre\n- reroute logistics\n- commission expedited emergent design\n\nActions deferred to after-action (not initiated as part of the live response):\n\n- reshoring or nearshoring\n- footprint redesign\n- new in-sourcing\n- ground-up redesign\n- contract renegotiation';

MERGE (s:LexSection {pointer: 'section:natural_disaster:escalation'})
SET s.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    s.role = 'escalation',
    s.heading = '5. Escalation',
    s.order_idx = 5,
    s.text = 'Three escalation levels apply: **Responsible Analyst** (authority: responsible_analyst); **Cross-functional Management** (authority: cross_functional_management); **Executive Leadership** (authority: executive_leadership). The level is set by the matching provision in Section 3. Higher levels are reserved for directly exposed high-risk suppliers, structurally critical suppliers, and disruptions that reach a shared source or spread across several paths simultaneously — situations where the disruption is likely to outlast the network\'s absorption capacity.';

MERGE (s:LexSection {pointer: 'section:natural_disaster:posture'})
SET s.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    s.role = 'posture',
    s.heading = '6. Strategic priority',
    s.order_idx = 6,
    s.text = 'The standing posture for natural disaster disruptions is **Rapid Reconfiguration**. Acute, shorter disruptions favour flexibility / contingent rerouting over standing redundancy (Tomlin 2006).';

MERGE (s:LexSection {pointer: 'section:natural_disaster:afteraction'})
SET s.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    s.role = 'afteraction',
    s.heading = '7. After-action',
    s.order_idx = 7,
    s.text = 'After the response, record the scenario, dispositions_taken, outcome. Any structural measures identified as necessary during the response — those that could not be executed within the recovery window — are passed to the resilience roadmap to be put in place before the next event. The record informs the next scheduled review of this standard.';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-NULL'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-NULL',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'routing',
    p.order_idx = 0,
    p.heading = '(NAT-NULL) Disruption outside network boundary',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 2. Activation and routing > (NAT-NULL) Disruption outside network boundary\n\nWhere the disruption does not intersect any path in the firm\'s supply network, or where all Tier-1 suppliers on any affected path carry LOW risk scores with none showing high downstream criticality, no immediate action is required. The assessment is logged and the relationship is maintained at existing terms. The response is to **maintain** the existing relationship, escalating to **Responsible Analyst**. Assessment for this scenario ends here.';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-DT'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-DT',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'routing',
    p.order_idx = 1,
    p.heading = '(NAT-DT) Deep-tier structural fallthrough — no Tier-1 supplier scored',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 2. Activation and routing > (NAT-DT) Deep-tier structural fallthrough — no Tier-1 supplier scored\n\nWhere no scored Tier-1 supplier sits on a disrupted path, yet the disruption either shares a sub-tier source across paths or runs across two or more paths, the exposure is structural rather than direct. The shared or multi-path structure represents a hidden concentration even without a directly affected Tier-1, and a contingency must be staged. Do not default to maintain simply because no Tier-1 is directly scored: the structural risk is real. The response is to **monitor** the supplier, escalating to **Cross-functional Management**. Assessment for this scenario ends here. *No Tier-1 scored - branch on structure + material, do not default to maintain.*';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-DT-NULL'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-DT-NULL',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'routing',
    p.order_idx = 2,
    p.heading = '(NAT-DT-NULL) Deep-tier with no structural concern',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 2. Activation and routing > (NAT-DT-NULL) Deep-tier with no structural concern\n\nWhere no Tier-1 supplier is on a disrupted path and neither a shared sub-tier source nor two or more disrupted paths are present, the disruption reaches into lower tiers without the convergence or breadth that would justify staging a contingency. The response is to **maintain** the existing relationship, escalating to **Responsible Analyst**. Assessment for this scenario ends here.\n\n**Pass 2 — Per-supplier evaluation.** If no routing provision fired, each Tier-1 supplier on a disrupted path is assessed individually against the provisions in Section 3.';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-R3'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-R3',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'supplier',
    p.order_idx = 0,
    p.heading = '(NAT-R3) Shared sub-tier convergence override',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 3. Decision logic > (NAT-R3) Shared sub-tier convergence override\n\nWhere two or more disrupted paths share a common lower-tier source, at least 2 supply paths are disrupted, and the supplier\'s composite risk score falls in the MEDIUM or HIGH band, the response is to **replace** the supplier, escalating to **Executive Leadership**. Permitted live actions: activate a pre-qualified alternate source, reroute logistics, and run scenario lever generation.';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-R1'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-R1',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'supplier',
    p.order_idx = 1,
    p.heading = '(NAT-R1) High-risk Tier-1 directly in the disrupted region',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 3. Decision logic > (NAT-R1) High-risk Tier-1 directly in the disrupted region\n\nWhere the supplier\'s composite risk score falls in the HIGH band and the supplier\'s primary site lies within the affected region, the response is to **replace** the supplier, escalating to **Executive Leadership**. Permitted live actions: activate a pre-qualified alternate source, reroute logistics, and intensify threat monitoring.';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-R5'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-R5',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'supplier',
    p.order_idx = 2,
    p.heading = '(NAT-R5) Medium-risk in-region supplier with high downstream exposure breadth',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 3. Decision logic > (NAT-R5) Medium-risk in-region supplier with high downstream exposure breadth\n\nWhere the supplier\'s composite risk score falls in the MEDIUM band, the supplier\'s primary site lies within the affected region, and the supplier\'s exposure breadth score is high, the response is to **replace** the supplier, escalating to **Executive Leadership**. Permitted live actions: activate a pre-qualified alternate source, reroute logistics, and run scenario lever generation. *A moderate-scoring in-region supplier feeding many downstream nodes is a single concentrated reroute exposure.*';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-R2'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-R2',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'supplier',
    p.order_idx = 3,
    p.heading = '(NAT-R2) High-risk Tier-1 outside the disrupted region',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 3. Decision logic > (NAT-R2) High-risk Tier-1 outside the disrupted region\n\nWhere the supplier\'s composite risk score falls in the HIGH band and the supplier\'s primary site lies outside the affected region, the response is to **monitor** the supplier, escalating to **Cross-functional Management**. Permitted live actions: intensify threat monitoring and run scenario lever generation.';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-MEDS'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-MEDS',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'supplier',
    p.order_idx = 4,
    p.heading = '(NAT-MEDS) Medium-risk supplier flagged by the disruption-type priority signal',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 3. Decision logic > (NAT-MEDS) Medium-risk supplier flagged by the disruption-type priority signal\n\nWhere the supplier\'s composite risk score falls in the MEDIUM band and the supplier\'s exposure breadth score is high, the response is to **monitor** the supplier, escalating to **Cross-functional Management**. Permitted live actions: activate a pre-qualified alternate source and intensify threat monitoring. *High ripple potential -> proactive contingency even at MEDIUM (Tomlin 2006).*';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-MED'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-MED',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'supplier',
    p.order_idx = 5,
    p.heading = '(NAT-MED) Medium-risk supplier',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 3. Decision logic > (NAT-MED) Medium-risk supplier\n\nWhere the supplier\'s composite risk score falls in the MEDIUM band, the response is to **monitor** the supplier, escalating to **Responsible Analyst**. Permitted live actions: intensify threat monitoring.';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-LOWS'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-LOWS',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'supplier',
    p.order_idx = 6,
    p.heading = '(NAT-LOWS) Low-risk supplier flagged by the disruption-type priority signal',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 3. Decision logic > (NAT-LOWS) Low-risk supplier flagged by the disruption-type priority signal\n\nWhere the supplier\'s composite risk score falls in the LOW band and the supplier\'s exposure breadth score is high, the response is to **monitor** the supplier, escalating to **Responsible Analyst**. Permitted live actions: intensify threat monitoring. *Watch structurally vital nodes even at LOW own-risk (Ivanov & Dolgui 2020).*';

MERGE (p:LexProvision {pointer: 'provision:NAT-LOW'})
SET p.rule_id = 'NAT-LOW',
    p.disruption_type = 'natural_disaster',
    p.pass = 'supplier',
    p.order_idx = 7,
    p.heading = '(NAT-LOW) Low-risk routine supplier — catch-all',
    p.text = 'Natural-Disaster Disruption — Supply-Chain Disruption Response Standard > 3. Decision logic > (NAT-LOW) Low-risk routine supplier — catch-all\n\nWhere the supplier\'s composite risk score falls in the LOW band, the response is to **maintain** the existing relationship, escalating to **Responsible Analyst**. Permitted live actions: intensify threat monitoring.';

